  "authoringNote": "C01: 2024-02-29 (a valid leap day) plus six calendar months is 2024-08-29; August has 31 days, so no clamping applies and the day is kept, not moved to the end of August. The final order on 2024-08-29 is on the inclusive bound, follows the encounter and shares SYN-PRAC-0001, so R04 passes with six citations. The receipt (2024-08-30T17:00:00Z) is after the order date span 2024-08-28T10:00Z to 2024-08-30T12:00Z (C06), so R05 passes. The case and explicit assessment date stay 2026-10-18 and the supplier interval 2026-01-01 to 2026-12-31 contains it; the older medical dates are synthetic arithmetic inputs only. No rule compares an order's age with the assessment date, no order-age limit is implied and no clinical or current-policy validity is claimed for an old order. R01, R02, R03, R07, R08 and R09 pass, R06 is qualified clinical review with five clinical citations and no administrative effect, and R10 is not applicable. No condition holds outside R06 and R10, every parent set is empty and the state is ready_for_review; human acceptance remains a separate action.",
